  "surface": "Source normals and source height control an opaque surface coating. No added snow volume, replacement primitive, texture image, bone or animation.",
  "memory": "Regional materials and uniforms are small additions. Each resident vegetation variant also owns instance matrices and a 256px render of the actual coated GLB for far display. These are extra GPU allocations; the source geometry and source textures are shared by object identity.",
  "visualReview": "Inspected all seven base models in the five-way comparison, including reverse, top and underside samples. Snow leaves the lower trunk and tent interior exposed and avoids the centre of a lit hearth. Ash darkens rock/wood; sand uses warm strata and dry plant tones. Coarse tree facets were visible with white snow, so snow trees use the detailed source mesh nearby and its actual rendered impostor beyond 14m.",
